    <h1>Accruals Workflow</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Month-end accruals from preview through approval to AH journal. Workflow-controlled, audit-trailed, configurable per cost center.</p>
    <div class="pill-row">
      <span class="pill">Cash Hub</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<nav class="feature-nav feature-nav-top"><a class="feature-nav-btn prev" href="feature-ah-journals.html"><span class="feature-nav-label">← Previous</span><span class="feature-nav-title">AH Journals & Manual Journal Batches</span></a><a class="feature-nav-pos" href="feature-library.html"><strong>8</strong> / 25 · all features</a><a class="feature-nav-btn next" href="feature-collections-cases.html"><span class="feature-nav-label">Next →</span><span class="feature-nav-title">Collections Cases (Aged Accrual Write-Offs)</span></a></nav>
  <div class="feature-hero-image">
    <img loading="lazy" src="screens-onedigital/cashhub-accruals-batches.png" alt="Accruals Workflow representative screen">
    <div class="caption">
      <span>Representative screen</span>
      <a href="screens-onedigital/cashhub-accruals-batches.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full-size →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <p>Accruals close the gap between <em>commission earned</em> and <em>commission received</em>. The carrier owes the brokerage money for policies sold; that revenue is recognized in the period earned, not in the period the carrier writes the check.</p>
<p>The accruals system has four moving parts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Preview</strong> (<code>/Accruals/Preview</code>) — read-only dashboard of computed accruals with variance vs. prior month</li>
<li><strong>Batches</strong> (<code>/Accruals/Batches</code>) — committable workflow surface; create batch, edit lines, submit, approve</li>
<li><strong>Configuration</strong> (<code>/Accruals/Configuration</code>) — admin: cost center inclusion toggles + per-broker ignore flags</li>
<li><strong>Process trigger</strong> (<code>/Accruals/ProcessBatches</code>) — on-demand batch computation outside the nightly automation</li>
</ul>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>The problem it solves</h2>
    <p>Accruals are the controller's monthly nightmare. The 12-month rolling-average calc is straightforward in principle; the complications come from data quality (a product with no transaction history, a broker on leave, a cost center being sunset). Without a workflow surface, accruals are spreadsheet-driven and error-prone.</p>
<p>The Unite accrual flow makes the math visible (Preview), the overrides controlled (Batches with workflow status), and the policy explicit (Configuration). The nightly automation does the heavy lifting; humans review + adjust + approve.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>What the user actually does</h2>
    <ul><li><strong>Morning of the close:</strong> controller opens <code>/Accruals/Preview</code>. Variance indicators show what changed vs. prior month. Anomalies flagged for investigation.</li><li><strong>Investigate variance:</strong> drill into a row, see the per-product detail. Decide if it's a real change or a data-quality issue.</li><li><strong>Open Accrual Batches:</strong> find the relevant batch (one per cost center × month). Edit individual lines to apply overrides where needed.</li><li><strong>Submit</strong> the batch → workflow transitions NotSubmitted → Submitted. Manager approves → status becomes Approved. Approved batches handoff to AH via the integration function.</li><li><strong>Configure once a year:</strong> which cost centers participate in accruals, which brokers are flagged 'Ignore for Accruals' (terminated, on leave, etc.).</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>Key screens</h2>
    <div class="key-screens">
      <p style="margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--slate); font-size: 14.5px;">Click any screen to open its dedicated guide — what's on the page, where the data comes from, vocabulary, and customer Q&amp;A.</p>
      <div class="key-screens-grid"><a href="screen-cashhub-accruals-preview.html">Accruals Preview →</a><a href="screen-cashhub-accruals-batches.html">Accrual Batches →</a><a href="screen-cashhub-accruals-config.html">Accruals Configuration →</a><a href="screen-cashhub-accruals-broker.html">Broker Config →</a><a href="screen-cashhub-accruals-process.html">Process Accrual Batches (on-demand) →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>Business value</h2>
    <div class="value-callout">
      <p>Month-end accruals go from 'a multi-day fire drill done in Excel' to <strong>a 1-2 day workflow with explicit ownership at every step</strong>. Variance investigations happen early (Preview catches anomalies before commitment); the close becomes predictable.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <details class="tech-anchors">
    <summary>Technical anchors (entities, handlers, integrations)</summary>
    <div class="tech-body">
      <p><strong>Entities:</strong> <code>AccrualBatch</code>, <code>AccrualLine</code>, <code>AccrualCostCenterConfiguration</code>, <code>Broker.IgnoreForAccruals</code>, <code>AccrualPeriodConfig</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Pages:</strong> <code>AccrualPreview.razor</code>, <code>AccrualBatches.razor</code>, <code>AccrualBatchLines.razor</code>, <code>AccrualBatchTrigger.razor</code>, <code>AccrualConfiguration.razor</code>, <code>AccrualBrokerConfigs.razor</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Calculation:</strong> <code>IAccrualsCalculationService</code> runs a 12-month rolling-average per product.</p>
<p><strong>Queries:</strong> <code>GetAllAccrualBatchesQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetAccrualBatchHeaderQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetPagedAccrualGroupsQueryHandler</code>, <code>PreviewAccrualLinesQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetAccrualVarianceAnalysisQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetAccrualVarianceProductDetailQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetPagedAccrualBatchLinesQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetAccrualGroupLinesQueryHandler</code>, <code>RecalculateSingleAccrualLineQueryHandler</code>, <code>GetPagedAccrualBrokerConfigsQueryHandler</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Commands (shared library):</strong> <code>CreateAccrualBatchCommandHandler</code>, <code>TriggerAccrualBatchProcessingCommandHandler</code>, <code>SaveAccrualOverrideCommandHandler</code>, <code>ApplyFinanceTerminationToAccrualLinesCommandHandler</code>, <code>UpdateBrokerIgnoreForAccrualsCommandHandler</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Outbound integration:</strong> <code>AccrualsOverrideToAHHandoff</code> / <code>Polling</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Automation:</strong> <code>ProcessAccrualsBatchByCostCenter</code> Azure Function (nightly).</p>
<p><strong>Policies:</strong> <code>Accruals.CanView</code>, <code>CanManageBatches</code>, <code>CanApprove</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <section class="feature-block">
    <h2>Related features</h2>
    <div class="related-features"><a href="feature-ah-journals.html">AH Journals</a><a href="feature-collections-cases.html">Collections Cases</a></div>
  </section>

